On Feb 26, 9:51 am, Tapio Peltonen <tap...@utu.fi> wrote:
> On 2008-02-26, purple arcanist <ejg_...@yahoo.com> wrote:
>
> > I would like some help with my wizard.  How do I survive in the early
> > game?  Once, I survived, but that is because I started with a ring of
> > regeneration and a ring of slow digestion.  Should I just not get
> > within melee range (that is hard), use Elbereth, or what?
>
> Wizard is probably the easiest class to survive in the early game.

It probably isn't.  Even experienced serial ascenders have a lot more
trouble with early wizards than with early Valks, Barbs, Sam, etc.
But with the right strategy they can survive at a high rate.

> You have the Force bolt, and occasionally also a second useful spell. Try to
> pick up daggers and throw them at enemies, too (get skilled in dagger!).
> (Wielding a dagger instead of the quarterstaff is not a bad idea either.)
> Letting the initial pet help might also be a good idea, but I just seem to
> get my initial pets killed early on in just about every game.

The pet is a huge help as long as it survives, and taming replacements
isn't tough.  Daggers are just great, but stick with the staff until
you find an enchanted dagger or get your skill way up (definitely
_throw_ daggers, try to avoid melee, and practice with daggers in
melee against non-threatening foes).

> The usual beginner advices apply: Avoid melee, throw/shoot projectiles
> instead. Try to get some decent armor early on. Never be burdened. Try
> to keep an escape route clear whenever in close combat.

Use force bolt as needed, especially if foes line up.  But don't be
afraid to put on some mithril and run with a dagger-tossing strategy
for a while until you get your PW up and find some decent other armor
and leather/studded leather.

> Do not worry too
> much about hunger, you can always (if you haven't done something stupid)
> count on your god filling your stomach when you are weak. Still, don't
> wear rings you don't need.

Usually past the very very early game, it's more of a pain to get
hungry enough to eat all the corpses you want for intrinsics.  But
very early on, yeah,  avoid rings unless they're rather useful.


